  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TUI Academy Thailand. Protection and economic empowerment of youth in tourism in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY. The main objective will be to improve child protection, in particular preventing (sexual) exploitation of children and youth through multistakeholder engagement (including DCI-ECPAT), promoting due diligence processes among the private sector and by offering youth sustainable, decent economic opportunities, in TUI&#x2019;s direct sphere of influence (TUI Hotels &amp; Resorts), via the TUI Academy approach. Plan International will be cooperating closely with Robinson Club resort in Khao Lak to offer disadvantaged youth with vocational training, life skills training, internship and a chance at decent work in the Robinson resort (or other comparable employers). The target will be 150 enrolled (at least 135 graduating, at least 120 in jobs) disadvantaged youth at risk of exploitation who are currently unable to access formal, decent employment due to lack of skills and opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
